  "id": "DrugBank_DB00860 - MONDO_8733",
  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Familial Glucocorticoid Deficiency through a shared pathway involving prednisone. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone, when used for conditions such as Autoimmune Hemolytic Anemia, Chronic Primary Adrenal Insufficiency, and Chondrocalcinosis, is associated with the induction of Familial Glucocorticoid Deficiency. This connection is supported by the observed indication links, which imply that prednisone, a glucocorticoid, may play a role in the metabolic or functional impairment seen in this condition. The recurring involvement of prednisone in these indications suggests a potential mechanism where glucocorticoid receptor dysfunction or metabolic dysregulation is linked to the deficiency. While the exact mechanism remains unclear, the evidence points to a possible dependency on glucocorticoids, which may be disrupted in Familial Glucocorticoid Deficiency, leading to the observed clinical associations.",
